<title>FRANCE: Fourth French beet test shows fall in yield.</title>
<headline>Fourth French beet test shows fall in yield.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's fourth 1996 sugar beet test showed a fall in sugar weight to 9.382 tonnes per hectare from 9.951 tonnes at the same point last year, the French sugar manufacturers' association SNFS said on Friday</p>
<p>The test showed an average sugar content of 17.21 percent compared with 16.98 percent in the fourth 1995 test.</p>
<p>The test was carried out on September 9. The fourth 1995 test was carried out on September 11.  </p>
<p>				 4th test 96   4th test 95   3rd test 96</p>
<p> Sugar per ha (tonnes)	9.382	   9.951	   7.647</p>
<p> Avge sugar content (pct)  17.21	   16.98	   15.87</p>
<p> No. of beets/ha	    101,700	 109,200	 100,800</p>
<p> Leaf/top wt/ha (tonnes)   37.425	  36.687	  37.085</p>
<p> Root wt per hare (tonnes) 54.528	  58.271	  48.198</p>
<p> Leaf/top to root weight    0.68	    0.63	    0.77</p>
<p> Rain in past 2 wks (mm)   27.30	   39.20	   40.70</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
